", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Rsc64G8bRQNRirrZXSqmfo", "tool": "rollback", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18589, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Rsc64G8bRQNRirrZXSqmfo", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 22621, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0185H4HvRfeQmUcEqgqnpdhq", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-api elevated errors after v5.1.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "payments-api started throwing errors after this morning's deploy of v5.1.0. It was unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Rolled back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, and the rollback is confirmed in all three regions. Follow-up needed: confirm recovery and find the root cause in v5.1.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 23221, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0185H4HvRfeQmUcEqgqnpdhq", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 23221, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0185H4HvRfeQmUcEqgqnpdhq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23221, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0157YttbGw3rpyraGANXPqMU", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 23521, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0157YttbGw3rpyraGANXPqMU", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 23521, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0157YttbGw3rpyraGANXPqMU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 28152, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened a SEV2 incident. The service has recovered.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service named \"payments.\" The affected one is `payments-api`, which was on v5.1.0 (this morning's deploy). It was unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Rollback:** I rolled `payments-api` back to v5.0.0 in all three regions. The release history only has v5.0.0 (healthy in production) and v5.1.0 (degraded), so v5.0.0 is the newest healthy one. This didn't need change-manager approval because v5.0.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Result:** The service now shows as healthy on v5.0.0 in all three regions, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 at SEV2 for `payments-api`, and on-call has been paged. It describes the bad deploy and the rollback, and lists confirming recovery and finding what's wrong in v5.1.0 as follow-ups.\n\nv5.1.0 shouldn't be redeployed until the cause is found and fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the current state of payments and its release history.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Wi5cL4ajoVLX8TwDr8YtN6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CSiTqn5mVfgQKeX9fqBTF3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "nam